questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-concurrency Spring Boot microservice intermittently throws `NullPointerException` or returns partially populated data during rule evaluation. The team recently added a double-checked locking lazy initialization pattern to a singleton bean:

java
@Component
public class DynamicRuleEngine {
    private RuleConfiguration cachedConfig;

    public RuleResult process(RequestContext context) {
        if (cachedConfig == null) {
            synchronized (this) {
                if (cachedConfig == null) {
                    cachedConfig = new RuleConfiguration(context.getTenantId());
                }
            }
        }
        return cachedConfig.execute(context);
    }
}


Under high load with multiple worker threads, threads occasionally see `cachedConfig` as non-null, but its internal fields inside `execute()` contain default/uninitialized values.
